@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+# MODULE — RAG engine (`backend/app/chat/**`, `llama_index_settings.py`)
+
+Everything that turns a question plus a set of documents into a streamed, cited answer.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Files
+
+| File | Responsibility | Key symbols |
+|---|---|---|
+| `chat/engine.py` | build the agent | `get_chat_engine`, `build_doc_id_to_index_map`, `index_to_query_engine`, `fetch_and_read_document`, `get_chat_history` |
+| `chat/messaging.py` | bridge LlamaIndex callbacks → anyio stream | `ChatCallbackHandler`, `handle_chat_message`, `StreamedMessage`, `StreamedMessageSubProcess` |
+| `chat/pg_vector.py` | pool-sharing vector store | `CustomPGVectorStore`, `get_vector_store_singleton` |
+| `chat/qa_response_synth.py` | custom QA/Refine prompts | `get_custom_response_synth` |
+| `chat/constants.py` | prompt + chunking constants | `DB_DOC_ID_KEY`, `SYSTEM_MESSAGE`, `NODE_PARSER_CHUNK_SIZE=512`, `NODE_PARSER_CHUNK_OVERLAP=10` |
+| `chat/utils.py` | human labels for tools/prompts | `build_title_for_document`, `build_description_for_document`, `_fallback_title`, `_fallback_description` |
+| `llama_index_settings.py` | global defaults | `_setup_llama_index_settings()` sets `Settings.llm`, `.embed_model`, `.node_parser` |
+
+Import-time side effects: `chat/engine.py:64` `nest_asyncio.apply()`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Object graph per conversation
+
+```
+ReActAgent(max_iterations=6, context=SYSTEM_MESSAGE, chat_history)
+└── QueryEngineTool "document_question_engine"
+    └── SubQuestionQueryEngine(use_async=True,
+                               question_gen=LLMQuestionGenerator(Gemini),
+                               response_synthesizer=custom QA/Refine)
+        ├── QueryEngineTool name=<doc A uuid>  desc="Annual report for …"
+        │     └── VectorStoreIndex.as_query_engine(similarity_top_k=3,
+        │              filters=MetadataFilters([ExactMatchFilter(db_document_id=uuid)]))
+        ├── QueryEngineTool name=<doc B uuid> …
+        └── …
+```
+
+All tiers use `settings.GEMINI_CHAT_LLM_NAME`; embeddings are configured globally in
+`llama_index_settings.py` and used by `VectorStoreIndex`.
+
+---
+
+## 3. `get_chat_engine(callback_handler, conversation)` step by step
+
+`chat/engine.py:181`
+
+1. `CallbackManager([callback_handler])` — the manager is threaded into every index/engine so all
+   events reach the SSE handler.
+2. `build_doc_id_to_index_map(...)` (`:112`):
+   - `vector_store = await get_vector_store_singleton()`
+   - `StorageContext.from_defaults(vector_store=vector_store)`
+   - per document: `VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store(...)`; on exception
+     `fetch_and_read_document(doc)` → `from_documents(...)` → `set_index_id(doc_id)`.
+   - ⚠ does **not** check that vectors exist for the doc (see `AGENTS.md §14.H`).
+3. `id_to_doc = {str(doc.id): doc}`.
+4. one `QueryEngineTool` per doc: `name = doc_id` (the LLM selects tools by name **and**
+   description), `description = build_description_for_document(doc)`.
+5. `response_synth = get_custom_response_synth(callback_manager, conversation.documents)`.
+6. `chat_llm = Gemini(model=…, api_key=settings.GOOGLE_API_KEY)`.
+7. `question_gen = LLMQuestionGenerator.from_defaults(llm=chat_llm)`.
+8. `SubQuestionQueryEngine.from_defaults(query_engine_tools, question_gen, response_synthesizer,
+   verbose=LOG_LEVEL=="DEBUG", use_async=True)`.
+9. single top-level tool `document_question_engine` with a deliberately broad description.
+10. `chat_history = get_chat_history(conversation.messages)`.
+11. `SYSTEM_MESSAGE.format(doc_titles=…, curr_date=utcnow %Y-%m-%d)`.
+12. `ReActAgent.from_tools(tools, llm, chat_history, verbose, context, callback_manager,
+    max_iterations=6)`.
+
+**Cost per question** (rule of thumb): 1 ReAct planning call + 1 question-generation call + N
+sub-answer calls + 1 synthesis (refine may loop) + N×retrieval embedding calls. A 3-document
+question is easily 6-8 Gemini calls.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Prompts
+
+### `SYSTEM_MESSAGE` (`constants.py:3`)
+Indian-financial-research persona; lists the selected document titles; mandates: always use tools,
+prefer document evidence, preserve units, disambiguate FY, do not fabricate, cite pages, decline
+off-topic questions; injects `{curr_date}`.
+
+### QA + Refine (`qa_response_synth.py:11`)
+Both templates restate the selected document list and the unit/FY/no-fabrication rules. Refine
+keeps the original answer when new context is useless. `structured_answer_filtering=False`.
+If you change chunking or models, re-read these prompts — they are the main defence against
+unit conversion drift.
+
+### `chat/messaging.py` nudge
+Every user question is prefixed with
+`"Remember - if I have asked a relevant financial question, use your tools."` (`messaging.py:145`).
+Removing it increases tool-skipping.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Vector store integration (`pg_vector.py`)
+
+```python
+class CustomPGVectorStore(PGVectorStore):
+    def _connect(self):           # :19
+        self._engine = create_engine(self.connection_string)   # sync engine (base-class paths)
+        self._session = sessionmaker(self._engine)
+        self._async_engine = app_engine                        # SHARED async pool
+        self._async_session = AppSessionLocal
+    async def close(self):        # :27
+        self._session.close_all(); self._engine.dispose(); await self._async_engine.dispose()
+    def _create_tables_if_not_exists(self): pass
+    def _create_extension(self): pass
+    async def run_setup(self):    # :39  CREATE EXTENSION vector + base.metadata.create_all
+    async def ensure_initialized(self): self._initialize()     # no DDL
+```
+
+`get_vector_store_singleton()` (`:66`) builds it once from `settings.DATABASE_URL` via
+`make_url(...)` and `from_params(host, port or 5432, database, user, password, table, embed_dim)`.
+
+Because it is a **module global with no lock**, two concurrent first calls in a worker can create
+two instances (last one wins) — harmless but worth knowing if you add async startup work.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Document titles / descriptions (`utils.py`)
+
+`build_title_for_document` → `"Reliance Industries (RELIANCE) Annual Report FY2025"`; falls back to
+`"Uploaded Document: <filename>"` or `"Uploaded Document"`.
+`build_description_for_document` → `"Annual report for Reliance Industries (RELIANCE), financial
+year 2025 (exchange: NSE)."`; falls back to `"Uploaded financial document: <filename>"`.
+
+Both tolerate missing/garbage metadata (`try/except` around `NSEDocumentMetadata.model_validate`).
+This text feeds the system prompt **and** the ToolMetadata ← the routing quality of the agent
+depends on it.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Callback events → sub-process rows
+
+| LlamaIndex event | Where it comes from | UI effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CONSTRUCTED_QUERY_ENGINE` (synthetic) | `messaging.py:137` | "engine built" step |
+| `LLM` | every Gemini call | thinking / synthesis steps |
+| `RETRIEVE` | vector search per doc | retrieval step |
+| `SYNTHESIZE` | response synthesizer | synthesis step |
+| `SUB_QUESTION` | sub-question engine, payload `EventPayload.SUB_QUESTION` = `SubQuestionAnswerPair` | Q/A + citations per document |
+| `AGENT_STEP` | ReAct loop | agent step |
+| `CHUNKING`, `NODE_PARSING` | ingestion | deliberately ignored (`messaging.py:39`) |
+
+`get_metadata_from_event` (`messaging.py:71`) only enriches `SUB_QUESTION`:
+`{"sub_question": QuestionAnswerPair(question, answer, citations).dict()}`.
+
+Adding a new streamed field: extend `get_metadata_from_event` + `schema.SubProcessMetadataKeysEnum`
++ the frontend's `MessageSubProcess`/`ResearchTrail` rendering.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Changing the model or retrieval
+
+| Change | Files | Caveats |
+|---|---|---|
+| Different Gemini model | `.env GEMINI_CHAT_LLM_NAME`, `engine.py:219` (explicit `Gemini(...)`) | both construct LLMs — keep them in sync |
+| Different provider | `llama_index_settings.py`, `engine.py:219-223`, `core/config.py` | `GOOGLE_API_KEY` env export must go too |
+| Top-k | `index_to_query_engine` (`engine.py:109`, `similarity_top_k=3`) | higher k ⇒ more context tokens, slower |
+| Chunk size | `constants.py:25-26` | requires re-index; no migration needed |
+| Embedding dimension/model | `.env` + `pg_vector.py` + recreate `data_pg_vector_store` | old rows become unusable |
+| New top-level tool | `engine.py:233 top_level_tools` | ReAct will route between tools; give a precise description |
+| More agent iterations | `engine.py:267 max_iterations=6` | latency grows |
diff --git a/docs/agents/modules/streaming.md b/docs/agents/modules/streaming.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..350a6e2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/agents/modules/streaming.md
@@ -0,0 +1,194 @@
+# MODULE — streaming (SSE) & the client transport
+
+Server: `backend/app/chat/messaging.py` + `backend/app/api/endpoints/conversation.py`.
+Client: `frontend/src/lib/api.ts` + `frontend/src/store.tsx`.
+
+Read `../WORKFLOWS.md §W3` for the full trace; this file is the mechanics.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Server: producer side (`chat/messaging.py`)
+
+```python
+class StreamedMessage(BaseModel):            # :22   cumulative answer text
+    content: str
+
+class StreamedMessageSubProcess(BaseModel):  # :26
+    source: MessageSubProcessSourceEnum
+    has_ended: bool
+    event_id: str
+    metadata_map: Optional[SubProcessMetadataMap] = None
+```
+
+`ChatCallbackHandler(BaseCallbackHandler)`:
+
+- `ignored_events = [CHUNKING, NODE_PARSING]` for both start and end (`:39`).
+- `on_event_start` / `on_event_end` **must be synchronous** (LlamaIndex API) and therefore do
+  `asyncio.create_task(self.async_on_event(..., is_start_event=…))` (`:51`, `:65`) — fire and
+  forget, no backpressure, exceptions are swallowed.
+- `async_on_event` (`:89`): builds `metadata_map`, maps `source = MessageSubProcessSourceEnum[event_type.name]`
+  (⚠ `KeyError` if LlamaIndex adds an event type the enum lacks), checks `self._send_chan._closed`
+  (private!), then `await self._send_chan.send(StreamedMessageSubProcess(...))` with
+  `ClosedResourceError` caught and logged.
+- `start_trace` / `end_trace` are no-ops (`:117`).
+
+`handle_chat_message(conversation, user_message, send_chan)` (`:128`):
+
+```
+async with send_chan:                       # closes the stream on exit
+    engine = await get_chat_engine(ChatCallbackHandler(send_chan), conversation)
+    send CONSTRUCTED_QUERY_ENGINE(has_ended=True, event_id=uuid4())
+    resp = await engine.astream_chat("Remember - …\n\n" + user_message.content)
+    async for text in resp.async_response_gen():
+        response_str += text
+        if send_chan._closed: return        # client gone
+        send StreamedMessage(content=response_str)
+    if response_str.strip() == "": send apology
+```
+
+⚠ `user_message` is a `schema.Message` instance built by the endpoint (not persisted yet);
+`user_message.content` is read directly.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Server: consumer side (`endpoints/conversation.py:112` `event_publisher`)
+
+```python
+send_chan, recv_chan = anyio.create_memory_object_stream(100)     # :110
+async def event_publisher():
+    async with send_chan:                                        # ⚠ second owner
+        task = asyncio.create_task(handle_chat_message(conversation, user_msg_obj, send_chan))
+        message_id = str(uuid4())
+        message = Message(id=message_id, conversation_id=…, content="",
+                          role=assistant, status=PENDING, sub_processes=[])
+        final_status = ERROR
+        event_id_to_sub_process = OrderedDict()
+        try:
+            async for obj in recv_chan:
+                if isinstance(obj, StreamedMessage):          message.content = obj.content
+                elif isinstance(obj, StreamedMessageSubProcess):
+                     # merge start/end on event_id, keep first created_at
+                     sub = MessageSubProcess(message_id=message_id, source=…,
+                                             status=FINISHED if obj.has_ended else PENDING,
+                                             metadata_map=obj.metadata_map)
+                     event_id_to_sub_process[obj.event_id] = sub
+                     message.sub_processes = list(event_id_to_sub_process.values())
+                yield schema.Message.model_validate(message, from_attributes=True).model_dump_json()
+            await task
+            if task.exception(): raise ValueError(...) from task.exception()
+            final_status = SUCCESS
+        except Exception:
+            logger.error("Error in message publisher", exc_info=True)
+            final_status = ERROR
+        message.status = final_status
+        db.add(user_msg_obj); db.add(message); await db.commit()
+        final = await crud.fetch_message_with_sub_processes(db, message_id)
+        yield final.model_dump_json()
+```
+
+Key properties
+
+- Channel capacity 100: if the client stalls, the producer blocks on `send` (backpressure) — no
+  unbounded buffering.
+- `OrderedDict` keyed by `event_id` gives stable ordering and merges start/end pairs.
+- `message.id` is generated by the endpoint (a `str`); SQLAlchemy's UUID type coerces it.
+- The final frame re-reads from the DB so ids/timestamps are real.
+- Nothing is persisted while streaming; only at the end (success **or** error).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Wire format
+
+- `EventSourceResponse` from `sse-starlette==1.6.5`; `sep` defaults to `\r\n`; ping every 15 s
+  (`DEFAULT_PING_INTERVAL`) as `: ping - <ts>` comments.
+- Frames carry **no event name** ⇒ browsers deliver them on the default `message` listener
+  (`es.onmessage` / `addEventListener("message")`).
+- Each frame's `data` is one JSON `schema.Message` (see `../API_REFERENCE.md §4`).
+- Content is cumulative, so a client can drop intermediate frames safely.
+
+Raw example (two frames, truncated):
+
+```
+data: {"id":"b1e0…","conversation_id":"6d8f…","role":"assistant","status":"PENDING","content":"","sub_processes":[{"source":"CONSTRUCTED_QUERY_ENGINE","status":"FINISHED","metadata_map":null,…}],…}
+
+data: {"id":"b1e0…", … "content":"Reliance's FY2025 consolidated revenue was","status":"PENDING", …}
+
+data: {"id":"b1e0…", … "content":"… full answer …","status":"SUCCESS", "sub_processes":[…],"updated_at":"…"}
+```
+
+---
+
+## 4. Client side today
+
+`frontend/src/lib/api.ts` exports:
+
+```ts
+export interface StreamHandlers {
+  onUserMessage, onAssistantCreated, onSubProcess(stepId, patch), onToken(token),
+  onDone({content, sources}), onError(message)
+}
+```
+
+`MockTransport.streamMessage` (`api.ts:195`) synthesizes everything with `setTimeout`s and
+returns a cancel closure. That is the code path in production today (`USE_MOCK = true`).
+
+`RealTransport.streamMessage` (`api.ts:415`) is **wrong for this backend**:
+
+| Issue | Detail |
+|---|---|
+| Query param | sends `?q=` — backend reads `user_message` |
+| Event names | listens for `sub_process` / `delta` / `done`; backend sends unnamed snapshot frames |
+| Snapshot vs delta | expects raw token strings; must diff `content` between snapshots instead |
+| Sources | expects `done.sources`; backend delivers citations inside `sub_processes[].metadata_map.sub_question.citations` |
+| Error handling | `es.onerror` fires the generic "Stream interrupted"; EventSource cannot inspect HTTP status |
+| Transport choice | `EventSource` cannot send `Accept: text/event-stream` or auth headers; a `fetch` + `ReadableStream` reader is more flexible (the README even claims this, but the code does not do it) |
+
+### What a correct adapter must do
+
+1. `fetch(`${BASE_URL}/api/conversation/${id}/message?user_message=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`,
+   { headers: { Accept: "text/event-stream" } })`, then parse `data: ` lines from
+   `response.body.getReader()` (handle `\r\n`, blank-line frame boundaries, `:` comment pings).
+2. Maintain `prevContent`; emit `onToken(snapshot.content.slice(prevContent.length))`.
+3. Map each `sub_processes[]` entry to the UI step model
+   (`source` → `llm|retrieval|rerank|parser`, `status PENDING/FINISHED` → `running/completed`),
+   keying steps by `event_id`, since the backend re-sends the whole array each frame.
+4. Flatten citations from every `sub_question` into `Source[]` with a stable `index` (1-based) and
+   attach them on `onDone`.
+5. Persist nothing locally: after `onDone`, `GET /api/conversation/{id}` gives the canonical,
+   reload-safe thread (the mock store keeps conversations in memory only).
+
+---
+
+## 5. Store integration (`store.tsx`)
+
+| Handler | Mutation |
+|---|---|
+| `onUserMessage` | append `msg`, set conversation `updated_at` |
+| `onAssistantCreated` | append placeholder |
+| `onSubProcess` | find the message containing `stepId`, `{...step, ...patch}` |
+| `onToken` | last assistant message: `status="streaming"`, `content += token` |
+| `onDone` | last assistant message: `status="completed"`, replace content, set `sources`, clear streaming/cancel |
+| `onError` | `status="failed"`, toast, clear streaming/cancel |
+
+`patchConversation` always returns a **new** array sorted by `updated_at` desc. Token patches run
+per chunk (1-2 chars), so this is the hottest React path in the app — keep the reducer shallow.
+
+`stopStreaming()` calls the returned cancel closure and clears `streaming`; the partially rendered
+message stays.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Testing streaming changes
+
+There is no automated SSE test. Manual loop:
+
+```bash
+# 1. backend running with a real conversation
+curl -N "localhost:8000/api/conversation/<ID>/message?user_message=What%20was%20FY2025%20revenue%3F"
+# 2. confirm persistence + status
+curl -s localhost:8000/api/conversation/<ID> | jq '.messages[-1] | {status, len:(.content|length), subs:(.sub_processes|length)}'
+```
+
+If you write a test, drive `handle_chat_message` with an `anyio` stream and a stubbed
+`get_chat_engine` (patch `app.chat.messaging.get_chat_engine`) — that is the cheapest way to pin
+the frame contract without Gemini.
